Package: biasratio
Title: Bias-Effect Ratio for Quantifying Residual Systematic Bias in Observational Studies
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Zhechun", "Zeng", , "zengzhechun@users.noreply.github.com", role = c("aut", "cre"))
  )
Description: Quantifies residual systematic bias in observational effect
    estimates using negative control outcomes. Building on the OHDSI empirical
    calibration framework ('EmpiricalCalibration'), the bias-effect ratio
    (BER) expresses the magnitude of the estimated systematic bias relative to
    the calibrated effect estimate, turning the binary verdict of a calibrated
    p-value into a continuous, interpretable diagnostic. Each estimate is
    classified as bias-dominated, competitive, or effect-dominated. Provides
    log-scale bootstrap confidence intervals, leave-one-out sensitivity
    analysis, negative control diagnostics, and 'ggplot2' visualizations
    designed for clinical audiences.
